//  Static
static variables(class variables) are useful for class-wide state and constants.
static variables aren't initialized until they're used

// final and const
If you never intend to change a variable, use final or const, either instead of var or in addition
to a type. A final variable can be set only once, a const variable is compile-time constant.
(const variables are implicitly final.)
Note : Instance variables can be final but not const
